                        ],
                        "form": "вероло́мстве"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2086faf2-8f81-4a06-89e8-928f04a083d9",
                        "entry_id": "79f6f38b-5b0a-3493-98eb-a686c53d17bc",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "вероло́мствах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f75225dc-05e7-3eaa-a1ed-47b43d5946f8",
                        "entry_id": "79f6f38b-5b0a-3493-98eb-a686c53d17bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойство по значению прилагательного вероломный; вероломный характер поступка, действия, поведения; также склонность к предательству, нарушению клятв"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "21846d24-e8ee-407c-95ee-b53c6d06eeb8",
                                "sense_id": "f75225dc-05e7-3eaa-a1ed-47b43d5946f8",
                                "text": "Его хитрость, его вероломство были по-мужичьи просты."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e30b39b4-6dd2-4bc4-babf-77bdd71bb8a2",
                                "sense_id": "f75225dc-05e7-3eaa-a1ed-47b43d5946f8",
                                "text": "По самоуверенности, глупости, ослиной тупости, копеечному вероломству, дикарской хитрости и ледяному охамлению он мировой уникум."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54edc8ce-d2c5-4450-8861-385750c61dbb",
                                "sense_id": "f75225dc-05e7-3eaa-a1ed-47b43d5946f8",
                                "text": "Родительскую любовь предают, многолетнее побратимство… Человеческому вероломству Волкодав давно уже не удивлялся."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cf631ea3-0ef9-3a07-acba-27f8013823db",
                        "entry_id": "79f6f38b-5b0a-3493-98eb-a686c53d17bc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "вероломный поступок; нарушение клятвы, обязательств"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6270bc9-932a-4c67-8aab-8a0bbd65d5cb",
                                "sense_id": "cf631ea3-0ef9-3a07-acba-27f8013823db",
                                "text": "Преемник Василия Димитриевича, Василий Васильевич, был человеком ограниченных дарований, слабого ума и слабой воли, но вместе с тем способный на всякие злодеяния и вероломства <…>."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6775cd5c-7feb-4bbe-b66f-12c11c769510",
                                "sense_id": "cf631ea3-0ef9-3a07-acba-27f8013823db",
                                "text": "А между тем из всех наших предательств и вероломств по отношению к союзникам наше отношение к Румынии должно особенно ранить сколько-нибудь чуткую совесть."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d37942c-a9fb-492d-83f1-7e391e416d13",
                                "sense_id": "cf631ea3-0ef9-3a07-acba-27f8013823db",
                                "text": "<…> Франция, устрашённая ростом прусского военного могущества и оскорблённая вероломством своего бывшего союзника Фридриха, переметнувшегося на сторону Англии, объявила себя защитницей Австрии."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6af0181f-0046-4d2c-965b-507829e61618",
                        "source_entry_id": "79f6f38b-5b0a-3493-98eb-a686c53d17bc",
                        "target_lang_word": "betrayal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "betrayal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e099f56-adbe-3f18-a87f-8de1beb56c45",
                                        "entry_id": "ed007d7e-8ad3-3ce7-a0bf-be3e50f842e5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of betraying."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11189700-7340-4b44-b318-a12d7aa58e64",
                                                "sense_id": "6e099f56-adbe-3f18-a87f-8de1beb56c45",
                                                "text": "But by the same token, an exclusive menu of betrayals is likely to be a starvation diet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "347a143f-66bf-4dd6-9265-40b30c96a3e7",
                                                "sense_id": "6e099f56-adbe-3f18-a87f-8de1beb56c45",
                                                "text": "The betrayal of our friends in Taiwan began with President Carter’s decision to terminate the mutual defense treaty with Taiwan that Congress had ratified in 1954."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4b1c89f-65df-4518-b9b4-fe06c05efd79",
                                                "sense_id": "6e099f56-adbe-3f18-a87f-8de1beb56c45",
                                                "text": "One of our own has joined with the alien. If you see him, do not hesitate to let him know what the Roekaar think of this betrayal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0cdeb735-0da6-460b-9dde-b8995f57764a",
                        "source_entry_id": "79f6f38b-5b0a-3493-98eb-a686c53d17bc",
                        "target_lang_word": "treason",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "treason",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                        "entry_id": "082937ed-ca24-3bd6-9baa-8e5c05ab9dce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The crime of betraying one’s own country."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b26e92cb-c38a-449f-9341-a1fe73d11d2d",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "Treaſon doth never [pro]ſper: what's the reaſon? / For yf yt [pro]ſper none dare call yt treaſon"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8a0fdf6-1484-4d1a-9106-80198bc0a467",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "Treason against the United States, shall consist only in levying War against them, or in adhering to their Enemies, giving them Aid and Comfort. No Person shall be convicted of Treason unleſs on the Testimony of two Witneſses to the same overt Act, or on Confeſsion in open Court."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fae402c-9f0b-4bbf-8dc5-958c5cc6c14e",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "If for every error and every act of incompetence one can substitute an act of treason, many points of fascinating interpretation are open to the paranoid imagination: treason in high places can be found at almost every turning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "96842da8-fa3f-4235-96ba-77731983f198",
                                                "sense_id": "9db7b9e5-1dd1-3ab4-a782-86dd643eb0e9",
                                                "text": "M. Vonel: 'Your involvement with a group calling themselves THE ORDER OF THE EZIC STAR has been uncovered. […] At least one EZIC member has confessed to receiving your help. This represents treason of the highest order. Goodbye inspector.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d745db41-536c-30b3-bd9c-104bb7f503af",
                                        "entry_id": "082937ed-ca24-3bd6-9baa-8e5c05ab9dce",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act of treachery, betrayal of trust or confidence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6dab9a17-c8f6-4224-aab5-3b1cee0e4e2e",
                        "source_entry_id": "79f6f38b-5b0a-3493-98eb-a686c53d17bc",
                        "target_lang_word": "treachery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "treachery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "064095ea-c8df-3f3a-a2be-5003241f0193",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deliberate, often calculated, disregard for trust or faith."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c314b71c-a56e-4763-85d2-bceaae6aaa42",
                                                "sense_id": "064095ea-c8df-3f3a-a2be-5003241f0193",
                                                "text": "Suddenly, in the midst of high-camp treachery and sleuthery, each character does a star turn, breaking out in song."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b68066a-2899-3b88-8f87-446be259e44f",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of violating the confidence of another, usually for personal gain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05ced43e-c308-3c38-a45d-9f2732d81ba4",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Treason."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a7dfb29-82aa-31d2-b340-59f4735f75df",
                                        "entry_id": "f60c7936-a8ca-384e-a4fa-dc1f5694100a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act or instance of treachery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e1f26cd-f8c3-43d7-9aa6-fa69d90c4f74",
                                                "sense_id": "9a7dfb29-82aa-31d2-b340-59f4735f75df",
                                                "text": "These submerged treacheries left an atmosphere. Even two such practised obliterators of their species as Bradly and Podson could not fail to note that each was secreting a certain reservation of opinion on the other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
